# Names and purpose only. Inject real values through the deployment secret store.
# APP_ENV — local, test, preview, staging or production; explicit for build/start.
# APPLICATION_MODE — foundation publishes only the closed informational shell; service enables customer capabilities and their production gates.
# The SUPABASE_* and PRODUCTION_SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF names below apply to service mode only; foundation reads none of them.
# APP_URL — canonical application origin, HTTPS for deployed environments.
# VERCEL_ENV — supplied by Vercel; must agree with APP_ENV.
# SUPABASE_URL — environment-specific hosted Supabase origin.
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — environment-specific public API key, kept server-side here.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — privileged server-only key; never expose to a client.
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF — identifier matching the Supabase origin.
# SUPABASE_ENVIRONMENT — data environment; must equal APP_ENV.
# PRODUCTION_SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF — production reference guard for project isolation.
# RATE_LIMIT_KEY_SECRET — at least 32 characters, for pseudonymous quota identities.
# RESEND_API_KEY — server-only email provider credential. Also sends organization invitations; without it (or EMAIL_FROM/APP_URL) the inviter gets a copy-the-link fallback, labelled as such. Auth emails (confirm, magic link, reset) go through Supabase, whose SMTP is set to Resend in the Supabase dashboard (D-017).
# EMAIL_FROM — verified sending identity.
# EMAIL_SANDBOX_RECIPIENT — mandatory recipient override for non-production email; previews send invitations here, never to the invitee.
# TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY — bot challenge site identifier (public; rendered in sign-up, sign-in after 3 failures, contact and the free generators).
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY — server-only bot challenge verification credential (siteverify). Either Turnstile key present switches verification on everywhere; only WAIVE_TURNSTILE with both keys absent switches it off.
# SENTRY_DSN — environment-specific error ingestion endpoint.
# PDF rendering runs in-process (src/lib/pdf) and there is no job queue yet, so no PDF worker or
# queue signing variables exist. Add them with the service that needs them, not before.
# PAYMENT_PROVIDER — disabled, stripe or paddle; provider onboarding is a launch decision.
# PAYMENT_API_KEY — server-only payment provider credential.
# PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET — server-only webhook verification credential.
# With PAYMENT_PROVIDER=stripe: PAYMENT_API_KEY is a restricted Stripe key with read access to Subscriptions and Charges (the webhook re-reads them); PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET is the endpoint's signing secret for /api/billing/stripe/webhook.
# Paid plans (P-002: proposed prices live in code but show only with PRICES_APPROVED=true). A plan has a buy button only when its five values below are valid and payments are open. <PLAN> is PRO or TEAM.
# PRICES_APPROVED — true only once the owner has approved PROPOSED_PRICES in src/lib/billing/plans.ts (D-020). Off (blank): no price anywhere and paid plans "Not available yet". On: the proposed prices show; a plan is buyable only with payments open and all five values below set.
# PRICE_<PLAN>_AMOUNT — the displayed price as a number, such as 29 or 29.50; must match the Stripe price the Payment Link charges.
# PRICE_<PLAN>_CURRENCY — ISO 4217 code in capitals, such as USD.
# PRICE_<PLAN>_INTERVAL — month or year.
# PAYMENT_LINK_<PLAN>_URL — the Payment Link's https URL, with no query string; the in-app upgrade button appends client_reference_id (the organization id).
# PAYMENT_LINK_<PLAN>_ID — the Payment Link id (plink_...); the webhook maps a paid checkout to its plan by this id, never by anything in the URL.
# INDEXNOW_KEY — proof of ownership for search submission.
# ANALYTICS_SITE_ID — environment-specific consent-aware analytics identifier.
# ENABLE_PAYMENTS — true only for an approved, configured provider.
# ENABLE_REGULATED_DOCUMENTS — true only with recorded regulatory approval. Offers the certificate of origin (D-008, D-025) in service mode only, and only together with REGULATED_DOCUMENTS_APPROVED=true and the LEGAL_COO_* review record below; anything missing keeps it refused and /api/ready reports regulated_documents: misconfigured. RUNBOOK.md, "Certificate of origin".
# LEGAL_COO_REVIEWED_BY — the named person who reviewed the certificate of origin wording and labels (src/lib/trade/certificate-of-origin.ts). Blank keeps it off.
# LEGAL_COO_REVIEWED_AT — YYYY-MM-DD of that review; a real date, not in the future. Blank or invalid keeps it off.
# ENABLE_TRANSACTIONAL_EMAIL — true only with approved, configured delivery.
# PAYMENTS_APPROVED — recorded payment, merchant and webhook readiness approval.
# REGULATED_DOCUMENTS_APPROVED — recorded legal/regulatory workflow approval.
# EMAIL_DELIVERY_APPROVED — verified sender and delivery controls approval.
# LAUNCH_APPROVED — recorded release checklist approval; required in production.
# WAIVE_TURNSTILE — true lets production service mode run without TURNSTILE_* keys (D-017); any configured key re-enables the challenge.
# WAIVE_SENTRY — true lets production service mode run without SENTRY_DSN (D-017); a configured DSN re-enables reporting.
# WAIVE_ANALYTICS — true lets production service mode run without ANALYTICS_SITE_ID (D-017); a configured ID re-enables analytics.
# WAIVE_INDEXNOW — true lets production service mode run without INDEXNOW_KEY (D-017); a configured key re-enables submission.
# Waived controls are listed by name in /api/ready under "degraded". Blank means not waived.
# --- Legal pages, contact, help and admin (D-009, D-018). Read per feature, outside the strict schema: a bad value disables that feature, never the deployment.
# LEGAL_ENTITY_NAME — registered name of the business that runs TradeDocs; printed on /privacy, /terms, /cookies. Blank shows "to be provided".
# LEGAL_ENTITY_COUNTRY — country the business is established in.
# LEGAL_ENTITY_ADDRESS — optional postal address shown on the legal pages.
# LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL — published contact/privacy address; also the recipient of contact-form notifications in production.
# LEGAL_GOVERNING_LAW — optional, e.g. "the laws of England and Wales"; the terms show "to be provided" until set.
# LEGAL_DATA_REGION — optional, the Supabase project's region as the privacy policy should state it.
# LEGAL_APPROVED_AT — YYYY-MM-DD the owner approved the legal text. Until set (with name, country and email), the pages show a draft banner, are noindex and stay out of the sitemap and llms.txt.
# PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAILS — comma-separated addresses allowed into /admin (exact match, confirmed accounts only). Blank means nobody; everyone else gets 404.
# CRON_SECRET — at least 32 random characters. Authenticates GET/POST /api/internal/purge-accounts (Authorization: Bearer <value>), the account purge for deletions past their 30-day grace. Blank or short closes the endpoint (503). Setting it schedules nothing: scheduling is an owner decision (RUNBOOK.md, "Account purge"). Admins can always run the purge from /admin/users.
# API_KEY_PEPPER — at least 32 random characters, server-only. The pepper organization API keys are hashed with (HMAC-SHA-256) for the public REST API (/api/v1, Team plan, D-025). Blank or short switches the API and key creation off (503; /api/ready reports api_reason) and nothing else. Changing it revokes every existing key at once (RUNBOOK.md, "API keys"). Generate with: openssl rand -base64 48
# CHAT_PROVIDER — live chat vendor for the help panel. Only "none" exists; any other value is treated as none until a vendor is approved and implemented.
# --- Official lookups (D-025). Read per feature, outside the strict schema.
# CSL_API_KEY — server-only trade.gov subscription key for the Consolidated Screening List API (developer.trade.gov), sent as the subscription-key header. Blank or malformed: /tools/denied-party-screening says it is not available, links the official CSL search, is noindex and unlisted, and /api/tools/denied-party answers 503. The HS code lookup needs no key.
# --- E-signature through Dropbox Sign (D-025). Server-only; read per feature, outside the strict schema: a bad value disables e-signature alone. Blank key means "E-signature not available yet" and nothing claims it.
# DROPBOX_SIGN_API_KEY — the Dropbox Sign account's API key (Settings → API). Also the key that verifies callback event hashes. Never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# DROPBOX_SIGN_CLIENT_ID — optional API app client id; applies that app's branding and callback URL. Blank sends from the account and uses the account callback URL.
# DROPBOX_SIGN_TEST_MODE — "true" makes production send test (non-binding) requests too. Every non-production environment always sends test requests, whatever this says.
# --- Accounting integrations (D-025). Read per feature, outside the strict schema: a provider is off ("Not connected — not available yet") unless its id, secret, INTEGRATION_TOKEN_KEY and APP_URL are all valid; nothing else is affected. Setup: RUNBOOK.md, "Accounting integrations".
# QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_ID — Intuit developer app client id (Development keys reach sandbox companies only).
# QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_SECRET — server-only Intuit client secret.
# QUICKBOOKS_ENVIRONMENT — sandbox or production; blank means production when APP_ENV is production, otherwise sandbox.
# XERO_CLIENT_ID — Xero web app client id.
# XERO_CLIENT_SECRET — server-only Xero client secret.
# INTEGRATION_TOKEN_KEY — server-only 32 random bytes as base64 or hex (openssl rand -base64 32), one per environment. Seals stored provider tokens (AES-256-GCM) and signs OAuth state; rotating it requires every organization to reconnect.
